README.md:118:Logging in has no limit on attempts, by design. Checking a password takes deliberate effort, so on a public server a flood of login requests can slow the app down. If that becomes a problem, your reverse proxy can cap how many requests one address sends.
docs/user-stories.md:47:  - There is no limit on failed login or recovery-code attempts.
docs/user-stories.md:156:6. Given 20 wrong passwords in a row, when I then enter the correct one, then I'm logged in. There's no limit on attempts.
docs/user-stories.md:168:3. Given a wrong recovery code, or a username that doesn't exist, when I reset, then a clear message is shown and no password is changed.
docs/user-stories.md:170:5. Given many wrong recovery codes in a row, when I then enter the right one, then the reset works. There's no limit on attempts.
